{{!
    @template mod_datalynx/field_location_app

    Display of a datalynxfield_location field in the Moodle App.

    The app runs none of the plugin's JavaScript, so no map is drawn: the address is shown
    with a link that opens directions to it in the maps app of the device.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * address - The stored address text.
    * mapurl - Link that opens directions to the place, empty without coordinates.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "address": "Bruno-Marek-Allee 5, 1020 Wien",
        "mapurl": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/directions?engine=fossgis_osrm_car&route=%3B48.228712%2C16.391983"
    }
}}
<div class="datalynx-location datalynx-location--app">
    <p class="datalynx-location__address">{{address}}</p>
    {{#mapurl}}
        <p class="datalynx-location__maplink">
            <a href="{{mapurl}}" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">
                {{#str}}openinmaps, datalynxfield_location{{/str}}
            </a>
        </p>
    {{/mapurl}}
</div>
